; Four lights, three of them leaning on defaults. Read each against
; the `sjon effective` line under it.
;
;   cat examples/plugins/variant-defaults/plugin.sjon \
;       examples/plugins/variant-defaults/example.sjon | sjon effective - --no-project

(anchor :name origin)

; Nothing written. `:kind` defaults to `point`, which selects the
; `point` variant, whose `:range` then defaults too:
;
;   (light :kind point :intensity 1 :range 10)
(light)

; The discriminant written, the variant's keys omitted. `:reach`,
; `:angle` and `:aim` all materialize, and `:aim origin` resolves
; against the anchor above:
;
;   (light :kind spot :intensity 1 :reach 20 :angle 45 :aim origin)
(light :kind spot)

; An author value always wins over a default, on a variant key as on a
; common one. `:angle 30` stays; the other two spot keys fill in:
;
;   (light :kind spot :angle 30 :intensity 1 :reach 20 :aim origin)
(light :kind spot :angle 30)

; `sun` declares no defaults and one required key, so this form is
; complete as written and gains only the common `:intensity`:
;
;   (light :kind sun :direction [0 -1 0] :intensity 1)
(light :kind sun :direction [0 -1 0])

; The lines NOT written here, both `unknown_key` on `:range`:
;
;   (light :kind spot :range 5)      ; `:range` belongs to `point`
;   (light :range 5 :kind point)     ; ahead of the discriminant
;
; A default is a fallback for an omitted declared key. A key the
; validator does not accept at its position is not declared there, so
; no default makes it legal.
